DesOS phone approval of administrator actions
=============================================

A phone paired with this computer through DES Connect can approve a sudo
command instead of you typing your password. It is OFF on a fresh system and
stays off until an administrator turns it on. Your password always keeps
working, and the first sign-in after starting the computer always needs it.

Turning it on
-------------
1. In your desktop session, enrol the phone's key and allow approvals:
     des-connect-ctl phonekey-status              (find the device ID)
     des-connect-ctl phonekey-enrol DEVICE_ID     (confirm on the phone)
     des-connect-ctl phonekey-set DEVICE_ID approve on
2. As root, record that key for the system and add the PAM rule:
     sudo desos-phonekey enable --user YOUR_NAME
   Compare the fingerprint it prints with the one on the phone.
3. Keep that root shell open and test in another terminal:
     sudo -k true
   Decline on the phone once and check the password prompt still appears.

Turning it off
--------------
     sudo desos-phonekey disable            (everyone; PAM files restored)
     sudo desos-phonekey disable --user X   (one user)
     desos-phonekey status

If you lose the phone: unpair it in DES Connect AND run
"desos-phonekey disable --user YOUR_NAME". Unpairing alone stops requests
reaching the phone, but the system record is only removed by disable.

What to know
------------
* The phone shows the exact sudo command and signs it; the signature is
  checked by root against the key recorded in /etc/desos/phonekey/users.
  A program running as you cannot change that key or the text you are shown.
* sudo remembers a successful authentication for a few minutes on the same
  terminal, exactly as it does after a password. Later commands in that
  window are not shown on the phone.
* polkit (graphical "Authentication required" dialogs) is not included by
  default: PAM is not told which action is being authorised, so the phone
  could only say "an administrator action". Add it deliberately with
  "--service polkit-1" if you accept that.
* After 3 declined or unanswered requests the phone is not asked again for
  10 minutes. Settings: /etc/desos/phonekey/phonekey.conf
* Every request and decision is logged to the auth log and to
  /var/log/desos-phonekey.log.
* Example PAM files are in /usr/share/desos/phonekey/pam. They are examples;
  let the tool make the edit.
